{"body": {"model": "jev-1.14.0", "state": {"network_description": "THE OBSERVATION\nThe network sees a 10 x 10 grid. Rows are numbered 0 (top) to 9 (bottom) and columns 0 (left) to 9 (right). The outer ring of cells (row 0, row 9, column 0 and column 9) is a wall border; the playable area is the inner 8 x 8 cells (rows 1-8, columns 1-8).\nEach cell has 5 binary channels (0 or 1):\n  channel 0  agent: the cells the player controls\n  channel 1  moving objects: things other than the agent that move\n  channel 2  reward targets: things that give reward\n  channel 3  obstacles: cells the agent cannot enter or that end the episode (the wall border is always here)\n  channel 4  previous frame: the cells that were in channel 0 or channel 1 on the previous step\nThe observation is flattened to 500 numbers. Input number i = (row * 10 + column) * 5 + channel; for example input 0 is (row 0, column 0, channel 0), input 4 is (row 0, column 0, channel 4), input 5 is (row 0, column 1, channel 0) and input 499 is (row 9, column 9, channel 4).\n\nTHE ACTIONS\nThe network outputs 5 numbers (logits), one per action; the action is sampled from the softmax of these logits:\n  action 0  no-op\n  action 1  up (toward row 0)\n  action 2  down (toward row 9)\n  action 3  left (toward column 0)\n  action 4  right (toward column 9)\n\nTHE NETWORK\nA policy network (multilayer perceptron) with 500 inputs, two hidden layers of 32 units with tanh activations, and 5 outputs:\n  h1 = tanh(x @ W1 + b1)          W1: 500 x 32, b1: 32\n  h2 = tanh(h1 @ W2 + b2)         W2: 32 x 32,  b2: 32\n  logits = h2 @ W3 + b3           W3: 32 x 5,   b3: 5\nRow i of W1 holds the weights from input i to the 32 hidden units; column j of a weight matrix belongs to unit j of the next layer. 17,253 parameters in total. It was trained with reinforcement learning (PPO) to maximise the reward of a game played on this grid.", "weights": {"representation": "lossy deterministic summary of parameters, not full weights", "definitions": {"grid": "Each 10x10 grid uses original row and column coordinates 0–9. Each cell aggregates its 32 outgoing W1 weights.", "interior": "Row and column summary arrays cover indices 1–8, excluding the known border.", "output_distance": "Mean absolute difference between two W3 action columns, over all 32 hidden units; biases excluded.", "limitations": "Absolute magnitudes discard signs and hidden-unit alignment. Weight magnitude is not causal importance; biases alone are not action probabilities. No activations or forward passes are available."}, "input_channels": {"agent": {"cell_mean_absolute_weight": [[0.052531249999999995, 0.06978125000000002, 0.04734375, 0.04196874999999999, 0.049624999999999996, 0.05278124999999999, 0.05403124999999999, 0.05674999999999999, 0.06515624999999997, 0.044000000000000004], [0.046375000000000006, 0.8841874999999999, 0.054, 0.0465, 0.045281249999999995, 0.06184375, 0.05593749999999999, 0.05746875, 0.04506250000000001, 0.05059375000000001], [0.036312500000000004, 1.0261874999999998, 0.057406250000000006, 0.04615625, 0.046375, 0.04240624999999999, 0.040906250000000005, 0.05062499999999999, 0.041843750000000006, 0.05315625], [0.04628125000000001, 0.58171875, 0.05571875000000001, 0.04959375000000001, 0.06118750000000001, 0.05162499999999999, 0.04634375000000001, 0.049937499999999996, 0.05921875, 0.06549999999999999], [0.04206249999999999, 0.3965000000000001, 0.04725000000000001, 0.06425, 0.057437499999999996, 0.05753125, 0.0521875, 0.060593749999999995, 0.04268750000000001, 0.05156249999999999], [0.06096875, 0.48234374999999996, 0.05078125, 0.046125, 0.05181249999999999, 0.060375, 0.05171874999999999, 0.05409374999999998, 0.046093749999999996, 0.05828124999999998], [0.03975, 0.6739687500000001, 0.050374999999999996, 0.05043750000000002, 0.05434375, 0.053062500000000005, 0.03949999999999999, 0.04321874999999999, 0.056312499999999995, 0.04834374999999999], [0.043437500000000004, 0.7715312499999999, 0.043062500000000004, 0.05059375, 0